hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18999","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Sinan, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by him while he was milking, and said: Leave what calls the milk."
"19112","Waki and Abu Muawiya said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, he said: My family sent me with a milch camel, and Abu Muawiya said with a she-camel in milk, to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I brought it to him and he ordered me to milk it, then he said: Leave the caller of the milk. Abu Muawiya said: Do not exhaust her."
